{"Frontend uses wrong i18n key 'user.email.invalid' for blocked email error message when backend uses 'user.email.blocked', creating inconsistent UX": 0.43697044253349304, "OAuth/social login flows (Facebook, Twitter, CAS, etc.) do not validate blocked emails - no explicit BlockedEmail check in social login pathway allows bypassing email blocks": 0.5275862812995911, "change_email endpoint bypasses all email validation including BlockedEmail check - users can change their email to a blocked address that would have been rejected at signup": 0.7847838997840881, "Email lookup in BlockedEmail.should_block? is case-sensitive, allowing bypass by using different capitalization (e.g., 'Spam@Example.com' bypasses block on 'spam@example.com')": 0.9250519871711731, "Invite creation lacks blocked email validation - needs investigation whether invites should be rejected at creation, redemption, or both": 0.1063736230134964, "Email change validation path needs investigation - unclear if User validator runs on changed emails or is skipped depending on ActiveRecord dirty state": 0.058871012181043625, "User.create_for_email raises unhandled exception on blocked emails instead of returning validation response, affecting invite and admin creation flows": 0.7899697422981262, "EmailValidator class may never be loaded despite being referenced in User model - validator requires explicit loading or Rails autoloading to discover it, potentially rendering blocked email feature non-functional": 0.5772319436073303, "Missing guard for undefined result.values.email in error response - code checks result.values but not result.values.email, causing pushObject(undefined) which breaks the contains() check for blocking emails": 0.7088068127632141}